Feedback: **Feedback on Attempt 1 (8.4 ms, about 240 GFLOP/s):**

1. **Per-call allocation and page faults.** Each call `aligned_alloc`s about 8 MB of fresh pages for Ap and Bp, so every run pays thousands of first-touch page faults. Keep the buffers in static storage and grow them only when n increases, so repeated benchmark runs reuse warm, mapped memory.

